--TEST--
`$uri->path` answers a `string` for every reference the grammar admits, where the other six readers each answer `null` somewhere — RFC 3986 § 3.3's path is not optional, and `""` is a path rather than the absence of one — spec § 12
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Six of `Core\Uri`'s seven component readers are typed `?string` (or `?int`);
// `path` alone is `string`, because RFC 3986 § 3.3 makes the path the one
// component every reference has. That is a claim about a whole grammar, not
// about a line, so it is asserted by *counting* absences over a corpus that
// reaches every shape § 4.1 admits: a member that answered `null` for the
// pathless-looking `http://a` would still print plausibly on every other row.
//
// The static half of the same claim needs no assertion and cannot have one:
// `$uri->path() == null` does not compile, `rule:expressions/object-identity-equality` refusing an equality
// whose two sides are statically disjoint, and `string $p = $uri->path();`
// needs neither an `as` nor a `??`. Both are visible below by their absence.

final class Show {
    // A `?string` rendered so that absent and empty are different characters.
    public static function some(?string $held): string {
        if ($held == null) {
            return "-";
        }
        return "[" . $held . "]";
    }
}

array<string> $corpus = [
    // With an authority, with and without anything after it.
    "http://a/b/c",
    "http://u:p@a:8080/b?q=1#f",
    "http://a",
    "http://a?q=1",
    "http://a#f",
    "file:///tmp",
    // A scheme and no authority: § 3.3's path-absolute and path-rootless.
    "http:/rooted",
    "http:g",
    "urn:isbn:1",
    // § 4.1's relative references, which have no scheme at all.
    "/relative",
    "//h",
    "?q=1",
    "#f",
    "",
];

int $noScheme = 0;
int $noUserInfo = 0;
int $noHost = 0;
int $noPort = 0;
int $noPath = 0;
int $noQuery = 0;
int $noFragment = 0;
int $emptyPath = 0;
int $pathInText = 0;
foreach ($corpus as string $written) {
    Core\Uri $uri = Core\Uri::parse($written);
    if ($uri->scheme() == null) { $noScheme = $noScheme + 1; }
    if ($uri->userInfo() == null) { $noUserInfo = $noUserInfo + 1; }
    if ($uri->host() == null) { $noHost = $noHost + 1; }
    if ($uri->port() == null) { $noPort = $noPort + 1; }
    if ($uri->query() == null) { $noQuery = $noQuery + 1; }
    if ($uri->fragment() == null) { $noFragment = $noFragment + 1; }

    // No `?string` here, so there is nothing to test for `null` — the counter
    // exists to be printed as the zero it must be, and the empty-path counter
    // is what the six above would have been measuring instead.
    string $path = $uri->path();
    if ($path == "") { $emptyPath = $emptyPath + 1; }
    if (Core\Str::contains($uri->toString(), $path)) { $pathInText = $pathInText + 1; }
}
echo "absent: scheme ", $noScheme, ", userInfo ", $noUserInfo, ", host ", $noHost,
     ", port ", $noPort, ", query ", $noQuery, ", fragment ", $noFragment,
     ", path ", $noPath, " of ", Core\Arr::count($corpus) as int, "\n";
echo "empty path ", $emptyPath, ", path present in the recomposed text ", $pathInText, "\n";

// The rows themselves, so the counts above are readable rather than asserted in
// the dark: `-` is absent, `[…]` is present and possibly empty. The last column
// is the one that never shows a `-`.
foreach ($corpus as string $row) {
    Core\Uri $each = Core\Uri::parse($row);
    echo Show::some($row), " scheme ", Show::some($each->scheme()),
         " host ", Show::some($each->host()),
         " query ", Show::some($each->query()),
         " path [", $each->path(), "]\n";
}
--EXPECT--
absent: scheme 5, userInfo 13, host 7, port 13, query 11, fragment 11, path 0 of 14
empty path 7, path present in the recomposed text 14
[http://a/b/c] scheme [http] host [a] query - path [/b/c]
[http://u:p@a:8080/b?q=1#f] scheme [http] host [a] query [q=1] path [/b]
[http://a] scheme [http] host [a] query - path []
[http://a?q=1] scheme [http] host [a] query [q=1] path []
[http://a#f] scheme [http] host [a] query - path []
[file:///tmp] scheme [file] host [] query - path [/tmp]
[http:/rooted] scheme [http] host - query - path [/rooted]
[http:g] scheme [http] host - query - path [g]
[urn:isbn:1] scheme [urn] host - query - path [isbn:1]
[/relative] scheme - host - query - path [/relative]
[//h] scheme - host [h] query - path []
[?q=1] scheme - host - query [q=1] path []
[#f] scheme - host - query - path []
[] scheme - host - query - path []
